{
  "date": "2026-10-18",
  "base_commit": "82a19033fc648934d94bf431db7949e1acaa0550",
  "scope": "Further Boolean-depth research in two existing works in progress; main papers and Lean source unchanged.",
  "new_results": [
    "An actual width-first critical parity sample lower bound through L <= c eta log(d)/log log(d), including posterior mixtures.",
    "A baseline-subtracted square-root entropy bound and matching excess-rate order for constants, dictators, and all parities over the stated depth range.",
    "A conditional-entropy/readout decomposition and a shallow product representation in the exact zero-directional-entropy case.",
    "Controlled covariance and readout transfer with polynomial depth amplification near the scalar baseline, without claiming generic low-rank compression.",
    "A depth-independent product bound for translation-invariant terminal kernels.",
    "Free Boolean kernel separation, a controlled pair-contraction construction, and a counterexample to depth-uniform stability based only on vanishing directional entropy.",
    "A normalized-action-only learning obstruction and a sufficient target-relative error-witness criterion.",
    "Constant-product depth padding and polynomial-cost majority/minimax closure for classifiers sharing their nonlinear feature map."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The general polynomial-depth Boolean learning theorem remains open.",
    "The new parity theorem is polynomial in dimension, not an exponential sample lower bound in teacher depth.",
    "A general critical-rate-to-product or finite-representation compression theorem has not been proved.",
    "The covariance transfer changes the controlled law; it does not assert stability of the same density formula or a generic low-rank approximation.",
    "Independent AI-agent mathematical review is not Lean verification."
  ],
